# Root-level context, used only by legacy-api's Docker build (server/Dockerfile.node),
# which needs to reach the shared rule files under client/src — see that
# Dockerfile's COPY steps for why. Every other service (client/, engine/,
# server-go/) builds from its own subdirectory and uses its own .dockerignore;
# this one keeps legacy-api's wider context from sending dependencies, build
# output and the other services' binaries to the daemon on every build.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.log
.git
client/coverage
server/coverage
engine/target
server-go/bin
server-go/api
